# No other faces or names

Hard rule for photos on diana’s dashboard (`my-dashboard`), including page backgrounds, home/dashboard tiles, pursuit cards, and the backgrounds gallery.

## Forbidden (generated / found / curated images)

- Anybody else’s **face** (photos, portraits, reflections, crowd shots, stock models)
- Anybody else’s **name** (printed, handwritten, letterhead, name badges, author lines, signatures, watermarks, captions)

## Allowed

- **Brand names she puts on a card** (e.g. Smile Set on the smile set card) — depict that brand by name; see `brand-named-cards`
- Diana’s own name / brand (e.g. Diana Jundi, Jundi Enterprises) when she asks for it
- Objects, places, documents, and scenes with **no** identifiable people and **no** third-party names

## User-provided screenshots (hard exception)

When Diana sends an **actual screenshot** (email, Handshake, messages, documents, etc.):

- Use it **as-is**
- **Never** redact, crop out, blur, regenerate, or replace faces/names
- Do **not** apply the “no other faces or names” rule to those screenshots

That rule only applies to images she asks you to **find, create, or generate**.

## When generating or choosing images

- Prefer still-lifes and environments with no people
- If text appears on papers/signs, keep it generic (titles, topics) — never invent other researchers’ or authors’ names
- If an existing **generated/found** asset has another person’s name or face, do **not** use it live; archive it and replace

## Everything page — vision collage

Day cards from Aug 26 onward use **vision collage** (see `everything-vision-collage` rule): full-bleed photo **sections** in a collage, not cards with black footers.

## Research proposals context

Research proposals on this board are in **psychology**. Generated photos should support that without naming or showing other people.
